WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.301
was playing Frisbee at summer camp.

2
00:00:17.661 --> 00:00:19.502
But she was thinking about Saturday.

3
00:00:20.383 --> 00:00:24.185
In just two days her family would go to see the town fireworks.

4
00:00:24.205 --> 00:00:29.448
"Mr. Dunn, I love the Fourth of July," Nina said.

5
00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:32.338
"Everything is red, white, and blue.

6
00:00:33.359 --> 00:00:35.561
And fireworks are so cool."

7
00:00:35.581 --> 00:00:39.144
"The Fourth of July is fun, isn't it?"

8
00:00:39.524 --> 00:00:40.545
Mr. Dunn said.

9
00:00:40.565 --> 00:00:44.168
"My family always has a big barbecue.

10
00:00:45.209 --> 00:00:47.251
My dad and brothers love to grill."

11
00:00:47.271 --> 00:00:50.434
"My dad loves to grill too!"

12
00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:51.475
Bobby said.

13
00:00:51.495 --> 00:00:57.300
"I always eat lots of watermelon on the Fourth," Izzie said.

14
00:00:58.344 --> 00:01:00.925
"You know what the kids in my family do on the Fourth?

15
00:01:02.186 --> 00:01:04.967
They make red-white-and-blue ice pops.

16
00:01:06.127 --> 00:01:09.729
Then they eat them while watching fireworks," said Mr.

17
00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:13.250
Dunn. "Red, white, and blue ice pops?

18
00:01:14.991 --> 00:01:17.192
I bet they're pretty," Nina said.

19
00:01:17.212 --> 00:01:23.974
"Yeah. They're pretty—and pretty easy to make," Mr.

20
00:01:24.014 --> 00:01:25.255
Dunn said, chuckling.

21
00:01:25.275 --> 00:01:27.556
"Can we make them at camp?"

22
00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.740
Nina asked.

23
00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:33.622
"Please? It's almost the Fourth of July."

24
00:01:33.642 --> 00:01:36.343
Mr. Dunn smiled.

25
00:01:36.364 --> 00:01:39.385
"That's a great idea, Nina.

26
00:01:40.425 --> 00:01:42.466
I'll bring in everything we need tomorrow."

27
00:01:45.527 --> 00:01:46.568
The next day Mr.

28
00:01:46.608 --> 00:01:50.729
Dunn brought in paper cups, wooden craft sticks, and three big bottles.

29
00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:53.090
Nina looked at the bottles.

30
00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:57.172
"Ooh, red juice," she said.

31
00:01:58.312 --> 00:02:00.133
"That's sweet strawberry juice.

32
00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:02.915
Made it myself," Mr.

33
00:02:02.975 --> 00:02:03.596
Dunn said.

34
00:02:03.616 --> 00:02:05.917
"Blue juice."

35
00:02:06.858 --> 00:02:08.399
Nina picked up another bottle.

36
00:02:08.419 --> 00:02:11.101
"Grape-blueberry blend.

37
00:02:11.981 --> 00:02:12.762
That's cool.

38
00:02:14.043 --> 00:02:14.963
And white juice.

39
00:02:15.804 --> 00:02:17.825
Wait a minute—white juice?"

40
00:02:17.845 --> 00:02:23.869
"It's actually coconut milk," Jason said, pointing to the label.

41
00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:25.931
"Have you had it before?

42
00:02:26.791 --> 00:02:27.272
It's good."

43
00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:29.380
Nina shook her head.

44
00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:32.561
"But I guess I'll try it in the ice pops."

45
00:02:34.162 --> 00:02:38.543
"This will be the easiest recipe you ever prepare," said Mr.

46
00:02:38.603 --> 00:02:44.705
Dunn. "First pour some blue juice into the bottom one-third of the cup."

47
00:02:44.725 --> 00:02:48.926
"The juice has to freeze before we can add the next layer, right?"

48
00:02:49.266 --> 00:02:50.226
Jason asked.

49
00:02:51.847 --> 00:02:53.467
"Exactly," said Mr.

50
00:02:53.527 --> 00:02:56.348
Dunn. "So let's get started."

51
00:02:57.344 --> 00:03:01.167
The kids filled the bottom of their paper cups with grape-blueberry juice.

52
00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:02.809
Then Mr.

53
00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.490
Dunn took the cups to the freezer.

54
00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:10.034
"We'll take those out in two hours," he said.

55
00:03:12.256 --> 00:03:14.398
The kids went outside for a nature walk.

56
00:03:16.419 --> 00:03:18.941
When they got back, it was time for the next step.

57
00:03:20.042 --> 00:03:22.004
"Now add the coconut milk.

58
00:03:23.105 --> 00:03:26.568
Fill the middle one-third of your cup," said Mr.

59
00:03:26.608 --> 00:03:28.785
Dunn. "And do it quickly.

60
00:03:29.765 --> 00:03:31.306
We don't want our blue to melt!"

61
00:03:35.429 --> 00:03:38.612
Mr. Dunn hurried to get the ice pops back into the freezer.

62
00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:43.315
Then the kids went outside for their Friday kickball tournament.

63
00:03:45.176 --> 00:03:49.419
In two hours they were back inside, ready to finish making their ice pops.

64
00:03:49.439 --> 00:03:55.163
"Last step: strawberry juice and craft sticks," Mr.

65
00:03:55.203 --> 00:03:55.824
Dunn said.

66
00:03:56.784 --> 00:04:01.086
"After you pour the strawberry juice, put your sticks in the cup.

67
00:04:02.146 --> 00:04:04.847
The coconut milk is still a little slushy.

68
00:04:05.928 --> 00:04:11.150
So you can gently push your stick through until it stands up straight," Mr.

69
00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:11.790
Dunn said.

70
00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:15.211
"Hurry, get these to the freezer!"

71
00:04:15.612 --> 00:04:16.292
Nina said.

72
00:04:19.713 --> 00:04:21.294
While they waited, Mr.

73
00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:23.355
Dunn read them a book about fireworks.

74
00:04:24.515 --> 00:04:26.316
Then they all painted fireworks.

75
00:04:27.508 --> 00:04:29.829
Finally the kitchen timer went off.

76
00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:32.711
It was time to take out the ice pops!

77
00:04:35.873 --> 00:04:39.815
Mr. Dunn peeled off the paper cups and handed a pop to each camper.

78
00:04:44.677 --> 00:04:46.558
Izzie said, taking a lick of blue.

79
00:04:47.939 --> 00:04:49.240
Nina licked the white part.

80
00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:52.041
"The coconut milk is good!

81
00:04:53.982 --> 00:04:54.723
Thanks, Mr.

82
00:04:54.763 --> 00:04:56.784
Dunn." Nina giggled.

83
00:04:58.029 --> 00:05:00.899
"Fourth-of-July fireworks, here I come!"
